{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/72817-power-costs-and-quantum-recovery","id":72817,"title":"Power Costs and Quantum recovery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T14:20:16-08:00","id":72817,"title":"Power Costs and Quantum recovery","content":"Now that you are making a new edition I trust some lesson learned from Scion and Exalted are going to be taken into Aberrant like stunts that aid in recovery of Quantum.<br /> <br /> But Quantum recovery aside I've found many Aberrant powers oddly costly in Quantum points, mostly those considering a mode of travel. Let's take flight for example. It costs 2 Quantum points per scene or per power+something turns. Is the latter really necessary? Why not just keep such costs at flat per scene costs? How often in does Superman have to stop flying because his running out of juice, or any flight capable superhero. And yes I know Aberrant is not strictly speaking a superhero game but their powers are straight from such genre so the comparison here is apt in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Personally in my games I haven't necessarily normally even taken any Quantum point costs from using things like flight or hyperspeed except in combat scenes where they pay the flat cost for the whole scene. I haven't found such cost policy to tip the balance neither here nor there. The powers where costs are more important like offensive powers, Quantum Bolt etc, and powers like Regeneration and Teleportation I have used the costs as these are actually things where you may run out of juice, except in X-Men movies where teleportation is used rather freely but such usage would considerably tip the balance as currently combat teleport is expensive as hell (3 Quantum per pop now watch X-Men 2's first scene again and count the size of Nightcrawler's Quantum pool, not to mention X-Men first class and Azazel's apparent pool if he were a Nova). Even with such greatly reduced prices Quantum tends to run out rather quickly in combat, especially without any stunting rules to help recover it. I haven't had time and opportunities to really play a lot of Aberrant games using stunt system but at my table I don't really think it would tip the balance too much.<br /> <br /> I'm interested to hear how others have house ruled costs or have you been strictly within the defined rules. Also if you happen to have ideas how you would like things to be handled now in the new edition please share them as there is at least some hope nowadays that we are being heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T20:09:44-08:00","id":72968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/72817-power-costs-and-quantum-recovery#post72817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you are making a new edition I trust some lesson learned from Scion and Exalted are going to be taken into Aberrant like stunts that aid in recovery of Quantum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new edition uses a new mechanics system, so house rules to patch the previous edition won't necessarily have anything to do with the new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}